    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25e347e4_a4c175d0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3277,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-03T16:29:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The NCT will stop sinking and we will lose power on the case of batteryless upon disabling AutoDischargeDisconnect.  We need to disable SNKEN from NCT CTRL_OUT in order to stop this clicking sound loop.  This happens after this disable of AutoDischargeDisconnect.  This is the only way I can find to get there.\n\n\t * 1. You set CC lines to Open/Open. This is physically happening on\n\t *    the CC line.\n\t * 2. Since CC is now Open/Open, the internal TCPC HW state machine\n\t *    is no longer in Attached.Snk and therefore our TCPC HW\n\t *    automatically opens the sink switch (de-assert the VBSNK_EN pin)\n\t * 3. Since sink switch is open, the TCPC VCC voltage starts to drop.\n\t * 4. When TCPC VCC gets below ~2.7V the TCPC will reset and therefore\n\t *    it will present Rd/Rd on the CC lines. Also the VBSNK_EN pin\n\t *    after reset is Hi-Z, so the sink switch will get closed again.",
      "parentUuid": "9e86f9c6_471d5532",
      "revId": "5403aa18365e4b479d5034982eacbc6b7de36217",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
